      en: "The Viking Ship Museum in Roskilde specializes in the display of five original Viking ships from the 11th century, recovered in 1962 from Roskilde Fjord. The ships had been sunk as a barrier to protect the city from attacks. The museum opened in 1969 and exhibits the ships in a purpose-built hall. Besides the originals, reconstructions are built and the history of Viking seafaring is conveyed. The museum also has an archaeological workshop and a ship garden. It is a leading center for experimental archaeology. The exhibition includes weapons, tools, and trade goods.",
